{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dropReports"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO"},{"kind":"text","text":"> { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait, without a bound, until they are read, so none is missed by reading late."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Drops are rare (each is a whole segment, or bytes recovery couldn’t read), so they don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pile up. The sequence ends once the store is gone and every report has been read."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads the reports at a time. The first iterator to read holds them until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iteration ends or it is released; a second reader meanwhile waits its turn, logging a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warning once, then reads on from the next report, so the first gets every report in order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A reader cancelled while it waits returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV11dropReports11AsyncQueues0F5QueueVyAA10DropReportOGvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"dropReports","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L163","fileName":"SegmentStore.swift"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dropReports"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","text":"AsyncQueue"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","text":"DropReport"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"]]},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"title":"SegmentStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"title":"DropReport","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","role":"symbol","title":"RecordStore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}]},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The reports or deliveries a library type makes, in the order it makes them, kept until they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are read; one reader at a time reads them."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncQueue"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"AsyncQueue","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncQueue"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"title":"Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistenc